salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: TAKE A CUT</b>
  Home > Reporting > Cuts > Take a cut
  --
  <b>TAKE A CUT</b> | Editable
  Four steps over one body. Nothing is fixed until the last press, and the press
  raises the authorisation with the body.
  (1) Kind and timepoint  (2) The body  (3) Review  (4) Take and authorise
  --
  <b>STEP 1: THE KIND AND THE INSTANT</b>
  {#
    Kind | What it fixes | Authorisation
    EOD | the centre's close, 16:00 Europe/London | required: reporting.cut_authorisation
    SOD | the centre's open, 08:00 Europe/London | not required: the take raises no request
    IPV | the close of the cut it is built on | required: reporting.cut_authorisation
    FLASH | an instant the process names | not required, and its values are indicative
  }
  The basis is the kind's declaration and not a choice made at the take.
  Close of the London centre: 06 Oct 2026 16:00Z | Timezone: Europe/London
  Cut time: CUT-LONDON-1600, read from the reference data and drawn, never typed.
  Label, derived from the kind, the scope and the date: EOD.ACME-LONDON.2026-10-06
  Scope: ACME London - LDN rates books, three books, one centre.
  A scope spanning two centres is refused here, not discovered at the assembly.
  --
  <b>STEP 2: THE BODY ASSEMBLED, AND THE GAPS THAT STOP IT</b>
  {#
    Part | State | What it holds
    The deals | CLOSED | 1,284 deals, 1,196 live, 88 expired or settled, 3 corrections
    The market data | OPEN | 6 of 7 sets resolved, 0 values
    The reference data | CLOSED | conventions v14, calendars v22, curves v31, settings v9
    The engine and the code | OPEN | ORE-Studio-7.1, wrapper v1.2.0, build none
    The taking identity | CLOSED | m.oduya, ACME London, 07 Oct 2026 08:15Z
  }
  <color:#eab308>3 GAPS STOP THIS BODY.</color> They do not fail the take: the draft keeps them.
  {#
    Part | Item | Why it stands | What closes it
    Market data | USD-SOFR-3M | no observation at or before the instant | publish a set
    Deals | IRS-2048-0117 | no version current at the instant | correct the deal
    Engine | the service build | nothing records the build | register the build
  }
  [ Cancel ] [ Save as a draft ]     <- no Take is drawn while a gap stands
  --
  <b>STEP 3: THE REVIEW AGAINST THE PREVIOUS CUT</b>
  {#
    What | Previous cut | This cut | Movement
    Deals in the population | 1,281 | 1,284 | +3
    Deals that left | - | 2 | +2
    Market data values | 3,908 | 3,912 | +4
    Curve configurations | v30 | v31 | moved
  }
  <b>It decides</b> which body one valuation reads, and it records the engine and the code.
  <b>It does not decide</b> the day's prices, the conventions, or how a product is priced.
  --
  <b>STEP 4: THE PRESS, AND THE STATE IT LEAVES</b>
  EOD: TAKEN. The body is frozen and request 4b7c1e02 was raised, of the kind
  reporting.cut_authorisation, in the queue of Finance. No run may price from it yet.
  <color:#ef4444>YOU CANNOT AUTHORISE THIS CUT.</color> Four eyes is the inbox's rule: a decision
  by the person who raised the request is refused.
  FLASH: IN USE. The body is frozen and no request is raised, because the kind requires
  none. A run may price from it now, and its results carry the indicative mark.
  --
  <b>THE CUT'S RECORD, IN EVERY STATE</b>
  {#
    Cut | Timepoint | State | Taker | Authoriser
    EOD.ACME-LONDON.2026-10-06 | 06 Oct 16:00Z | AUTHORISED | m.oduya | a.reyes
    EOD.ACME-LONDON.2026-10-05 | 05 Oct 16:00Z | SUPERSEDED | m.oduya | a.reyes
